{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDI0L1Jlc2lzdGFuY2UlMjBUaGV5JTIwRm91Z2h0JTIwQmFjayUyMCUyODIwMjQlMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Resistance They Fought Back","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/rlhkWiQT95aYSNvVo6ecnoKNtfS.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/6ellQaU5naSeSgBt8sozfJXKYhp.jpg","description":"We’ve all heard of the Warsaw Ghetto Uprising, but most people have no idea how widespread and prevalent Jewish resistance to Nazi barbarism was. Instead, it’s widely believed “Jews went to their deaths like sheep to the slaughter.”  Filmed in Poland, Lithuania, Latvia, Israel, and the U.S., Resistance – They Fought Back provides a much-needed corrective to this myth of Jewish passivity. There were uprisings in ghettos large and small, rebellions in death camps, and thousands of Jews fought Nazis in the forests. Everywhere in Eastern Europe, Jews waged campaigns of non-violent resistance against the Nazis.\n\nReleased 12 Apr 2024 · United States of America · Language: English · 90 min\nStudio: Leading Edge Productions, Lone Wolf Media\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"2024","genres":["Documentary","History","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"5.0","runtime":"90 min","cast":["Joel de la Fuente","Lisa Loeb","Andrew Kishino","Mark Zeisler","Julie Benko","David Rosenberg","Corey Stoll","Dianna Agron"],"director":["Paula S. Apsell","Kirk Wolfinger"],"released":"2024-04-12T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Paula S. Apsell","character":"Director"},{"name":"Joel de la Fuente","character":"Marcel Nadjari","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/xRDyGJpIYG0IFEv1nLD3C23WSeA.jpg"},{"name":"Lisa Loeb","character":"Ruzka Korchak","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/hNBhj3OSWjUopfVspS4BsT4o3Xj.jpg"},{"name":"Andrew Kishino","character":"Mordechai Anielewicz","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/f0qUMbSqsdANjSfsxOFeRyO22OB.jpg"},{"name":"Mark Zeisler","character":"Emanuel Ringelblum","p